==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[hunky]]

===Etymology===
According to [http://slate.msn.com/id/2110811/ Crying Wolof:Does the word ''hip'' really hail from a West African language?] by Jesse Sheidlower, the claim that this is derived from [[Wolof]] is erroneous.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
#(''US, pejorative'') A [[Hungarian]] (or, more generally, eastern European) labourer.
#(''US, slang'') A person of [[Hungarian]] or [[Yugoslav]] extraction.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}
#(''US'') All right; all square; in good order.

